With our new knowledge about iterators, we can change the build function to take ownership
of an iterator as its argument instead of borrowing a slice. We’ll use the iterator functionality
instead of the code that checks the length of the slice and indexes into specific locations. This
will clarify what the Config::build function is doing because the iterator will access the
values.
Once Config::build takes ownership of the iterator and stops using indexing operations that
borrow, we can move the String values from the iterator into Config rather than calling
clone and making a new allocation.
